## 4. Worker rules

1. Write only the assigned lane; do not modify root GOAL or another Worker's records.
2. After user authorization, create an active Goal referencing this file's absolute path.
3. Start execution only after the Worker and Reviewer configuration receipts are `enforced`; report any mismatch instead of silently falling back.
4. For each completed item, update execution, mark `implemented_pending_review`, and request the lane Reviewer.
5. Mark `approved` only after an explicit approval receipt.
6. Notify the Orchestrator about cross-lane issues, shared hotspots, pauses, or integration needs.

## 5. Completion conditions

- [ ] Every assigned item is `approved`.
- [ ] The lane-level integrated audit passes.
- [ ] Exact commit or artifact is recorded and the worktree is clean.
- [ ] The Orchestrator has been notified that integration may begin.
